Day 40: NoSQL Mini Project – Employee Directory

Topic:
Apply MongoDB CRUD operations, queries, and aggregation in a complete small project to build an Employee Directory.

Learning Objectives:

• Implement MongoDB CRUD operations in a real-world scenario.
• Use MongoDB queries and aggregation pipelines effectively.
• Build a functional Employee Directory system using MongoDB.

Activities / Deliverables:

• Create an Employee Directory database in MongoDB.
• Perform CRUD operations (insert, update, delete) on employee records.
• Write queries to filter and sort employee data.
• Build an aggregation pipeline to group employees by department.

Important Concepts:

• MongoDB CRUD operations: insertOne, insertMany, find, updateOne, updateMany, deleteOne.
• Query operators: $eq, $gt, $lt, $in, $and, $or, $not.
• Aggregation pipeline stages: $match, $group, $project, $sort.

SQL Syntax / Commands:

• db.collection.insertOne({name: "John", department: "HR"})
• db.collection.find({department: "HR"}).sort({name: 1})
• db.collection.aggregate([{$match: {department: "IT"}}, {$group: {_id: "$department", count: {$sum: 1}}}])

Real-world Use Cases:

• Managing employee records in organizations.
• Building directory systems for departments or teams.
• Analyzing workforce distribution across departments.

Tools / Tech:

• MongoDB 7
• MongoDB Compass

Summary:
Learned to apply MongoDB CRUD operations, query operators, and aggregation pipelines in a practical project. Built a functional Employee Directory system, demonstrating real-world application of NoSQL databases for managing and analyzing data.

